RData-backed bc2cpp payloads can own statically named Ruby ivars without
putting those names in the object's ordinary iv_tbl. The descriptors keep
mruby's ivar APIs and GC aware of those slots; unknown/dynamic names continue
to use the ordinary table.

A slot is an mrb_value unless its descriptor names another kind: bc2cpp's
typed slots keep a raw mrb_int/mrb_sym/mrb_bool/int-or-nil, which the ivar
APIs box on read and type-check on write, and the GC does not mark. Without
that, instance_variable_get/set, instance_variables, inspect and Marshal
could not see a typed ivar, and would read or write a table the generated
code never consults.

--- a/include/mruby/data.h
+++ b/include/mruby/data.h
@@ -25,8 +25,49 @@
 
   /** data type release function pointer */
